@startuml Composite-BOM-Solution-Objects
title THE SOLUTION as objects — 14 objects, 13 lines, one wheel required twice

skinparam objectAttributeIconSize 0

object "bicycle : Assembly" as bicycle {
  BIKE-CITY
  assemblyCost = $40.00
  totalCost() = $396.00
  totalWeightGrams() = 5950
}

object "frame : Assembly" as frame {
  FRAME-ASM
  totalCost() = $168.00
}

object "wheel : Assembly" as wheel {
  WHEEL-ASM
  totalCost() = $85.00
  totalWeightGrams() = 1535
}

object "hub : Assembly" as hub {
  HUB-ASM
  totalCost() = $13.70
}

object "saddle : Part" as saddle {
  SADDLE-CR
  unitCost = $18.00
}

object "rim, spoke, tire, tube : Part" as wheelParts
object "tubeset, fork, paint : Part" as frameParts
object "axle, bearing : Part" as hubParts

bicycle --> frame : qty 1
bicycle --> wheel : qty 2
bicycle --> saddle : qty 1
frame --> frameParts
wheel --> wheelParts
wheel --> hub : qty 1
hub --> hubParts

note right of wheel
  ONE wheel object, required twice —
  the quantity is on the EDGE, so there
  are not two wheel objects.

  This instance is still a tree. The MODEL
  allows a DAG: attach this same wheel to a
  spare wheelset and it gains a second
  parent. That is why "the parent" is a
  LIST, and why cache invalidation has to
  walk all of them.
end note

note bottom of bicycle
  A client calls totalCost() here.
  Each node adds its own cost to the
  sum of (child cost x quantity),
  bottoming out at the Parts.
end note

@enduml
